--TEST--
`status` is asked with the receipt `push` answered rather than with the row's number, so nothing has to carry the queue name beside it — `rule:concurrency/queue-four-members`, `rule:core-api/shape-rules`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A job is identified by a row *and* a queue, which is the pair
// `Core\Queue\Id` is the name for. A member taking a bare number would have to
// take the queue beside it or search every queue for the row, and sparing the
// caller the first is the whole reason `push` answers a class instead of the
// primary key it already has in hand.
Core\Queue::status(7);
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `Core\Queue\Id`, found `int`
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
